        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Rash"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Generalised polymorphic rash typical of varicella: erythematous macules, papules and 2–5 mm vesicles at various stages, including some crusted lesions and some umbilicated vesicles. Involves face, scalp, trunk and proximal limbs, densest on the trunk; not dermatomal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Rash onset and progression"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Rash started approximately 36 hours before assessment and spread from the trunk to the scalp, face and proximal limbs."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Skin tenderness and stinging"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Marked tenderness to light touch and stinging, especially on the torso under the bra line; pain reported as 6/10 when clothes rub."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
